June 1, 2006

DSS is pleased to announce DACS version 1.4.13.

This is primarily a bug fix and minor enhancements release.

Important new features include:
  + port to Apache 2.2
  + dacsauth, an initial version of a command line
    authentication program
  + a new authentication module, local_cas_authenticate,
    for authenticating through the Central Authentication
    Service (CAS)

Note: shortly after release, a significant bug was found.  Please refer to
http://dacs.dss.ca/download.html for details and the fix.

DACS is security software - we urge all users to upgrade to the latest release.

DACS is:
  o a powerful role-based access control system that can apply flexible
    access control to virtually any web service request
  o enhanced Apache authentication and authorization
  o single sign-on for Apache
  o for script and application developers, able to provide access control
    and authentication functionality to almost any program or script
  o for Unix-type platforms, such as Linux, FreeBSD, and Solaris

DACS 1.4.13 is released under dual licensing terms (a GPL-compatible open
source license and a commercial license).

DACS is hosted on SourceForge at http://sourceforge.net/projects/dacs
For more information, please visit the DACS home page at http://dacs.dss.ca

--
** Barry Brachman, Ph.D.
** Distributed Systems Software, Inc.
** brachman@dss.ca

