Trying to startup the LUG in Erie PA again, below is the Invite that
was sent out on wplug-erie mailing list.

###
You're invited to become a part of something BIGGER, something more
than the
mundane world your apart of today, you're invited to Erie LUG!

Meeting place:
Panera Bread off of I-90
1935 Keystone Dr
Erie, PA 16509

Date/Time:
Sun. June 11th 1pm-2pm'ish
Head North off of I-90 on Peach St. Panera bread is behind Taco bell.

You're invited to a meet and greet. Linux Users of Erie and
surrounding
area's are welcome to join us at Panera Bread to share your
experience with
Linux , socialize with other people interested in Linux, and to,
hopefully,
help to re-establish a Linux Users Group in the Erie area.

Topics of discussion so far are:
Just a Meet and Greet of *nix Users in the erea.
A standard time/place to hold meetings.
Any input is more than welcome.

Bring a friend, if they are not a Linux User? come anyway, learn
something
new, and best of all meet new people!
###

Everyone is welcome to join, check out http://erielug.org for a google
maps link (site is not hosted by me, yet, but the admin was kind enough
to post the msg).

